(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[9 1 "// The module _thread (PY6f; Modules/_threadmodule.c): threads over goroutines under the GIL (thread_gil.go,"] [10 1 "// PYS10 (a)), locks and re-entrant locks whose waits release the GIL (on the main thread interruptible by a"] [11 1 "// signal's handler), thread handles (start_joinable_thread, join, _shutdown joining the non-daemon threads at"] [12 1 "// the end), thread identity, and _local, thread-local data: one dict per thread, swapped in at each access."] [21 1 "// pyLock is a lock: a token in ch when it is free (acquire receives it, release sends it back)."] [34 1 "// acquire takes the lock: at once when it is free; else, blocking, within timeout (negative: no limit)."] [56 1 "// pyRLock is a re-entrant lock: its owner's ident (0: none), the count, the lock under it."] [65 1 "// threadHandle is a thread's handle (ThreadHandle): its ident, its state, done closed when it ends."] [68 14 "// handleNotStarted, handleRunning, handleDone"] [71 15 "// by start_joinable_thread (joinable)"] [93 1 "// timeoutMax is TIMEOUT_MAX in seconds (PY_TIMEOUT_MAX / 1e6 on Linux)."] [96 1 "// lockAcquireArgs reads acquire(blocking=True, timeout=-1): blocking and the timeout (negative: none)."] [133 1 "// timeoutArg is a join's or a get's timeout: None or absent no limit (negative), else seconds."] [154 1 "// currentIdent is the running thread's ident."] [157 1 "// allThreads are the started threads that run, oldest first, with their idents (queue 220: faulthandler's dumps read"] [158 1 "// them from goroutines that do not hold the GIL, so under a lock of their own and not from threadInfos)."] [165 1 "// threadsNewestFirst are the threads as CPython's interpreter lists them: the newest first, the main thread last."] [179 1 "// threadIdentOf is t's ident as the registry holds it (the main thread's mainThreadIdent)."] [189 1 "// mainInterpThread is the main thread of the running interpreter (set by NewInterp)."] [214 1 "// shutdownHandles are the non-daemon threads' handles, joined by _shutdown."] [217 1 "// startThread runs fn(args) in a new thread under the GIL (thread_run): SystemExit ends it silently, another"] [218 1 "// exception goes to sys.unraisablehook."] [251 1 "// writeUnraisable is PyErr_FormatUnraisable: sys.unraisablehook called with the exception, the message and the"] [252 1 "// object, or, when it is the default hook, CPython's text on stderr."] [288 1 "// WaitForThreadShutdown is Py_FinalizeEx's wait_for_thread_shutdown: threading._shutdown() when threading was"] [289 1 "// imported, its error printed."] [308 1 "// localState is a _local's per-thread dicts and its constructor's arguments (localobject)."] [317 1 "// localDict makes o's dict the running thread's, made (and __init__ called again, as CPython's"] [318 1 "// _ldict) on the thread's first access."] [763 4 "// PyErr_SetInterruptEx: only a Python handler is tripped; on the main thread it runs at once (CPython's"] [764 4 "// next eval breaker check is at the call's return)"] [771 3 "// set_name and _get_name: the thread's name as pthread_setname_np keeps it on Linux, encoded in utf-8,"] [772 3 "// cut at a NUL and at _NAME_MAXLEN (15) bytes, read back by os.fsdecode's rule"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[104 34] [170 35] [170 43] [173 26] [183 35] [233 34] [234 29] [258 51] [273 101] [274 37] [275 48] [302 32] [329 21] [339 56] [340 70] [475 40] [494 50] [660 38] [741 34] [765 26] [797 43]]} (go/file "builtins_thread.go" :imports [


